    "['clock clock-id [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ptp interface ge-2/0/0 clock-identifier 3', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ptp interface ge-2/0/0 clock-identifier 3\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses `ptp` (Precision Time Protocol) for clock synchronization configurations\\n- The interface naming format changes to Juniper's style (`ge-2/0/0` instead of `GigabitEthernet2/0/0`)\\n- The `clock-id` parameter becomes `clock-identifier` in Juniper\\n- Juniper requires the configuration to be under the `protocols ptp` hierarchy\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ptp interface ge-2/0/0 clock-identifier 3'}]]": 1,
